module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.generic_application_admits_distinct_unit_variant_arguments

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data generic_application_admits_distinct_unit_variant_arguments: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "generic_application_admits_distinct_unit_variant_arguments" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "SUBJECT: unit variants of one closed coproduct used to distinguish generic applications. Source: module application; type Marker = First | Second; type Record<P> { n: Int }; fn take(q: Record<First>) -> Int { q.n }; fn probe(q: Record<Second>) -> Int { take(q: q) }. A value at Record<Second> is accepted at Record<First>; agreement of runtime record fields does not establish agreement of the authored arguments.",
    "BASELINE: 03a3b91fb4c1ea7e408df2cb484f475d75080a7f, archived compiler SHA256 8692902cd6540b0cd1bd5f73701c6a3910bb3c87a73110f8125b0c00cdbfa02b, invocation https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/8979a487-2456-41ac-a190-322814d49638. One source, six emitted Rust files, exit 0, two UnlistedImportUse advisories naming First and Second. The same binary's Out/Other generic foreign constructor also accepts at zero diagnostics; its Acc counterpart accepts at zero.",
    "CHANGED COMPILER, NOT A LANDED REF: generated optional application carrier binary d5507a4364962f95f744833e6618f81a6738f36f9be972582d43638bbff9e488, invocation https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/87880de7-9bd7-45db-87dd-5df73f30beae. The variant specimen still accepts one source/six files, now with the same two import advisories plus DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided at the direct argument. The SAME binary refuses Out/Other with located TypeMismatch and accepts Acc at zero diagnostics. Refusal is reachable; it does not cover this argument-variant population.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT AND CURRENT RUNG: OutsideTheLadder for the accepted inhabitance fault. Advisory output is observability, not refusal. CEILING: unestablished. The diagnostic name says generic-formal undecidable, but no measurement establishes undecidability; do not use that name to declare a permanent ceiling.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a variant-to-declaration identity judgment at generic argument positions, consuming the declared variant identity and refusing the distinct-variant pair while admitting an identical-variant pair. Preserve the expecting-accept boundary probe until the repair flips it to a permanent refusing regression; the present acceptance is the defect, not desired language behavior.",
    "BOUNDARY: the generic_position_admits_a_foreign_constructor repair owns the concrete foreign coproduct shape Out<Int> / Other at a generic field or argument position; that sibling row is an unlanded sibling record not carried by #10567, and is not evidence that this unit-variant case is repaired. The direct_generic_application_admits_a_distinct_phantom_argument row owns bare marker declarations (type First and type Second), not unit variants; it is also an unlanded sibling record not carried by #10567. This row's distinct failure is Record<Second> supplied where Record<First> is declared, with both constructors belonging to one closed coproduct. The phantom_marker_type_argument_identity_witness renders these markers distinctly; it does not establish inhabitance. These explicit shapes prevent either sibling's rendering, bare-marker, or foreign-constructor result from being credited to this population.",
    "THE CEILING SENTENCE ABOVE IS NOW DISCHARGED BY MEASUREMENT, and this receipt exists to retire it rather than to widen this row's population. It said: the diagnostic name says generic-formal undecidable, but no measurement establishes undecidability, so do not use that name to declare a permanent ceiling. A four-arm fixture now establishes that the name is NOT a limit.",

    "THE INSTRUMENT IS test.claim.argument_shape_at_a_declared_position_probe_test, named rather than transcribed (DESIGN section 6) and landing with this receipt. It hands the compiler four sources through compile_dag_diagnostic_census and folds each to a blocking-diagnostic count; re-derive with claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/argument_shape_at_a_declared_position_probe_test.dag over the four function names it declares. Its arms differ in exactly one term at a time: the declared position is CONCRETE or GENERIC, and the argument is an obviously wrong String or an unapplied nullary function returning the declared type.",

    "WHAT THE COMPARISON SHOWS: the same String is REFUSED at the concrete position, located and typed, and ACCEPTED at the generic one.",

    "SO REFUSAL IS REACHABLE AND GENERICITY IS NOT THE REASON IT DOES NOT FIRE. One argument, one shape, two declared positions, two different answers. A String inhabits Map<K, V> for NO instantiation of K and V, so the mismatch is decidable WITHOUT deciding the generic, and the checker demonstrably decides exactly this shape one arm over. WHAT THE INSTRUMENT CAN AND CANNOT SEE, stated so this comparison is not read as more than it is: blocking_count folds census_blocking_rows, and DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided carries GateAdvisoryTypecheck, so no arm here counts that class and nothing here reports what that diagnostic did or did not say at either position. The measured facts are the two blocking counts alone.",

    "WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT ESTABLISH, because this row forbids borrowing evidence across populations and that boundary is respected here. The fixture's population is ARGUMENT SHAPE (a String where a Map is declared), not this row's VARIANT IDENTITY (Record<Second> where Record<First> is declared). Shape mismatch is decidable from the argument alone; variant identity may not be, and nothing here says it is. What transfers is strictly the ceiling, and by the weaker route the instrument actually supports: one decidable shape is REFUSED at a concrete formal and ACCEPTED at a generic one in the same run, so genericity alone is not what makes a mismatch undecidable, and this row may no longer treat a generic position as a permanent undecidability ceiling on that ground. This says nothing about what any advisory diagnostic reported, which no arm measures. The rung and the trigger stand as written.",

    "AND A SECOND ARM OF THE FIXTURE FOUND A SHARPER HOLE THAT IS NOT THIS ROW'S SUBJECT: an_unapplied_function_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused hands the CONCRETE formal an unapplied function -- empty_map rather than empty_map() -- and the compile is silent, while a_string_at_a_concrete_position_is_refused refuses a String at that identical position in the same run. That is a decidable mismatch admitted where the checker is demonstrably deciding, and it has its own home in unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position rather than a receipt here.",

    "THE EXPECTING-ACCEPT BOUNDARY PROBE THIS ROW ASKED TO BE PRESERVED NOW EXISTS AND IS NAMED HERE, because it landed in a neighbouring lane that did not know this row existed. The trigger above says: preserve the expecting-accept boundary probe until the repair flips it to a permanent refusing regression. The instrument is test.claim.marker_argument_not_consulted_witness_test, arm inline_distinct, named rather than transcribed (DESIGN section 6). Re-derive with claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/marker_argument_not_consulted_witness_test.dag over the four function names it declares. That arm hands the compiler unit variants of ONE closed coproduct at a generic argument position with no alias at either end, declares expect_blocking false, and therefore REDS IF THE REPAIR EVER LANDS -- which is exactly the permanent refusing regression this row wants, arriving before the repair rather than after it.",

    "WHAT THAT WITNESS ADDS THAT THIS ROW DID NOT OWN, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It adds the CONTRAST that identifies the mechanism: two NAMED ALIASES over DIFFERENT markers refuse, and two NAMED ALIASES over the IDENTICAL marker ALSO refuse. Those two arms are not this row population and are not evidence about it -- they are nominal-head comparison, a different question at a different position. Taken with inline_distinct they establish only this: the refusal a reader observes between two aliases is tracking the NAME, so the accepted inline case is not an inconsistency in the checker but the same checker never consulting the argument at all. This row still owns the accepted inhabitance fault and its rung; the witness supplies the boundary probe and the discriminating contrast, and nothing here promotes the rung or widens the population.",

    "A CONSUMER-FACING CONSEQUENCE WORTH RECORDING WHERE THE DEFECT IS FILED, since it is how the defect reaches people who will never read this row. std.measure ApparentPower carried an annotation asserting that Watt and VoltAmpere do not typecheck against each other BECAUSE they are different dimensions, and that carrying both on one dimension would make them interchangeable. The conclusion is right and the mechanism is wrong: they refuse each other because they are two NAMES. A manager cited that paragraph to a worker as grounds for minting a Quantity arm to buy dimensional safety, which a marker does not buy. gunbc#11190 corrects the annotation to name the instrument instead. The lesson for this row is that an accepted-inhabitance fault does not stay in the type system: it becomes prose elsewhere claiming a wall that is not there.",

    "DISPOSITION IS SHARED: baseline already carries DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided and its non-blocking interpreter/advisory-discovery dispositions. The changed route does not add those classifier arms. Repairing this variant population does not authorize promoting the whole diagnostic: it also covers generic identity<T> on baseline. Any disposition change must enumerate its complete population, not borrow evidence from this one specimen.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
